{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/58","id":4687131639,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF1_z9w","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/58","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/58.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/58.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/58","number":58,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Credit the published geometric characterization of Fantappie denominators","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The exact unit-density Fantappiè denominator question is already characterized by Akopyan–Bárány–Robins, *Algebraic vertices of non-convex polyhedra*, Advances in Mathematics 308 (2017), 627–644 ([DOI 10.1016/j.aim.2016.12.026](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2016.12.026)). The reduced denominator contains precisely the factors associated with nonzero algebraic vertices, whose tangent-cone indicators are not signed sums of line-cone indicators.\n\nThis package matches that result to the original triangulation-intersection vertex convention, supplies the explicit pole calculation and finite cone-flipping interpretation, and preserves the origin exception: the factor for the origin is the constant 1. It credits the published authors and the transform identities of Gravin–Pasechnik–Shapiro–Shapiro. No new discovery is claimed.\n\nValidation: a separate adversarial source and mathematical review passed without required corrections. All 284 author exact assertions reproduce byte for byte; 6,463 independent exact controls cover cone flipping, cancellation, direct integration and normalization. The full author manuscript was read; no inaccessible publisher-typeset PDF is claimed as inspected.\n\nDisposition: already_solved, zero new substantive attempts. The adjacent decomposition questions, arbitrary densities and reconstruction algorithms are outside this target. Only this problem’s attempt folder is changed.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T07:07:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T07:13:05Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"be1a920b01f898b229cb28b16998127001867cee","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/58/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/58/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/58/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/465d771ec1ddc91877e8d9db51ed59aea1b0d97d","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-30002298","ref":"dot/math-30002298","sha":"465d771ec1ddc91877e8d9db51ed59aea1b0d97d","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/Al